🚨 SNAP Cash Machine Exposed in Seattle

@nickshirleyy’s team went undercover near 12th and Jackson and documented EBT cards being sold for cash. At Lam’s Seafood a $120 charge for Spam and sushi let the balance be converted on the spot. A guard’s gun was taken in the resulting street fight and the crew had to leave.

Seattle police have already identified this trafficking pattern, tied it to the same market, and filed charges. The cash-out rate undercuts the purpose of the program and leaves legitimate SNAP recipients short.

@GovBobFerguson @MayorofSeattle @AGOWA this is happening in your city and state (if you even care).

@USDA @SecRollins @USDA_FNS the video shows benefits being turned into cash in real time. A coordinated state and federal review of the retailers and the street network is the minimum response if the goal is protecting the people the program is supposed to serve.

#SNAPFraud #EBTTrafficking #Seattle #LamSeafood #ProtectSNAP
